**Resubmitted: deviation (T4C), preferred-level cure.**

Repair made in operative language: the granting sentence now reads "…**Company may terminate** this Agreement or any Statement of Work **for convenience upon thirty (30) days** advance written notice to Contractor…", with the additive nature carried by a leading "In addition to the foregoing rights," rather than an interrupted "may also terminate". This keeps the customer-alias subject, the verb, and the convenience trigger contiguous in the operative grant.

Preferred elements, all in one inserted § 6(c):
1. Company convenience termination of the Agreement or any SOW;
2. 30 days' advance written notice;
3. pro-rata refund of prepaid fees for the post-termination period;
4. express bar on Contractor convenience termination while any SOW is outstanding.

§ 2, § 6(a) (mutual 15-day gap-period right) and § 6(b) (breach mechanics, payment through the effective date, Works-in-progress assignment) are untouched; no extras, deletions, or dangling references.
